4. StartupAppTask Investigation

StartupAppTask warranted additional review because it executes the legitimate Windows binary:

%windir%\system32\rundll32.exe

with the following argument:

Startupscan.dll,SusRunTask

The complete Scheduled Task XML was exported and reviewed.

Findings

The task contained:

Microsoft Windows task path
Startupscan.dll referenced from the Windows system directory
Microsoft-associated task metadata
Standard Windows security configuration
No suspicious external executable
No PowerShell execution
No command shell execution
No script execution
No unusual user-writable execution path
No randomized executable name

Although rundll32.exe is a legitimate Windows binary that can be abused by attackers, the observed usage was consistent with Windows startup application scanning.

Assessment

🟢 Likely Benign

